---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SpecCurve from '../components/SpecCurve.astro';
import DataFlow from '../components/DataFlow.astro';
import GlossaryTerm from '../components/GlossaryTerm.astro';
---

<Layout title="Methodology | Kulturkampf Research">
	<main class="container">
		<header class="page-header">
			<span class="eyebrow">Identification & Strategy</span>
			<h1>Econometric Framework</h1>
			<p>A rigorous approach to identifying the demographic impact of secular institutional shocks.</p>
		</header>

		<article class="monograph">
			<h2>1. The Identification Strategy</h2>
			<p>
				The primary challenge in identifying the effect of the Kulturkampf is that religiosity itself is endogenous to economic development. To overcome this, I utilize the **1871 religious cross-section** as a baseline for treatment intensity, interacting it with the exogenous timing of the May Laws (1873).
			</p>
			
			<div class="formula">
				{`$$BirthRate_{it} = \\alpha + \\beta(CathShare_i \\times Post1873_t) + \\mu_i + \\delta_t + \\Gamma X_{it} + \\varepsilon_{it}$$`}
			</div>

			<p>
				Where $\mu_i$ represents county <GlossaryTerm term="Fixed Effects">fixed effects</GlossaryTerm> and $\delta_t$ represents year fixed effects.
			</p>

			<h2>2. The Data Journey</h2>
			<p>
				The dataset is constructed from the **Galloway Prussia Database**, harmonizing over 40 years of vital statistics and census records. 
			</p>
            
            <DataFlow />

			<div class="method-callout">
			<ul class="method-list">
				<li><strong>Spatial Units</strong>: 452 Prussian counties (Kreise).</li>
				<li><strong>Temporal Coverage</strong>: 1862–1914 (Annual panel).</li>
				<li><strong>Outcomes</strong>: Crude Birth Rate (CBR), Legitimate vs. Illegitimate Births, and Infant Mortality.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>3. Addressing the "War Shock"</h2>
			<p>
				The Franco-Prussian War (1870–1871) caused a significant temporary drop in fertility due to mobilization. To ensure our Kulturkampf results are not biased by the war recovery, I re-estimate the baseline model while **excluding the years 1870–1872**. The results remain robust and statistically significant.
			</p>

            <SpecCurve />

            <div class="code-link-box">
                <div class="code-icon">
                    <code>py</code>
                </div>
                <div class="code-text">
                    <h4>Modular Analysis Pipeline</h4>
                    <p>The analysis is performed using a custom Python package. Check the <code>src/analysis</code> directory for the full TWFE implementation.</p>
                    <a href="https://github.com/AntonEbsen/Demography" target="_blank">View Python Source</a>
                </div>
            </div>
		</article>
	</main>
</Layout>

<style>
	.page-header {
		margin-bottom: 4rem;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
		padding-bottom: 3rem;
	}

    .eyebrow {
        color: var(--accent);
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 0.2rem;
        font-size: 0.8rem;
        margin-bottom: 1rem;
        display: block;
    }

	h1 {
		font-size: 4rem;
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}

    .page-header p {
        font-size: 1.4rem;
        font-family: var(--serif);
        font-style: italic;
        opacity: 0.8;
    }

	.monograph {
		max-width: 800px;
	}

	h2 {
		font-size: 2.2rem;
		margin-top: 4rem;
		margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
	}

	.formula {
		background: #000;
		padding: 3rem 2rem;
		margin: 3rem 0;
		border-left: 4px solid var(--accent);
		text-align: center;
		font-size: 1.3rem;
		border-radius: 4px;
        color: var(--accent);
        overflow-x: auto;
	}

	.method-callout {
		background: rgba(212, 175, 55, 0.05);
		padding: 2.5rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--border);
		margin: 3rem 0;
	}

	.method-callout h3 {
		font-size: 1.2rem;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.1rem;
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}

	.method-list {
		list-style: none;
		margin: 2rem 0;
	}

	.method-list li {
		padding: 1rem 0;
		border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.05);
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 1rem;
        font-size: 1.1rem;
	}

	.method-list li::before {
		content: '■';
		color: var(--accent);
		font-size: 0.8rem;
	}

    .code-link-box {
        margin-top: 5rem;
        display: flex;
        gap: 2rem;
        background: #000;
        padding: 2rem;
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        align-items: center;
    }

    .code-icon {
        background: var(--surface);
        padding: 1rem 1.5rem;
        border: 1px solid var(--accent);
        color: var(--accent);
        font-weight: bold;
    }

    .code-text h4 {
        font-size: 1.2rem;
        margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }

    .code-text p {
        font-size: 0.9rem;
        margin-bottom: 1rem;
        opacity: 0.7;
    }

    .code-text a {
        color: var(--accent);
        text-decoration: none;
        font-weight: bold;
        font-size: 0.8rem;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 0.1rem;
    }
</style>
